  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "The dominant finding is config_007 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, multimodal) achieving 0.706 accuracy, a massive jump over all other experiments (~0.51–0.54). The critical uncertainty is whether this gain is driven by the scvi_n200 RNA encoder itself or by its specific interaction with the image modality in fusion. Config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_018 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool, 0.530). If config_005 also shows a large accuracy gain, the RNA encoder is the primary driver and subsequent experiments should exploit scvi_n200 across fusion/aggregation settings. If it remains near 0.53, the multimodal interaction is the key, redirecting effort toward fusion and image-encoder choices. Resolving this distinction is the highest-value information gain for the remaining budget, as it determines the entire direction of future experiments."
}

